{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00454","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"247.1572","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Meperidine is metabolized in the liver by hydrolysis to meperidinic acid followed by partial conjugation with glucuronic acid. Meperidine also undergoes N-demethylation to normeperidine, which then undergoes hydrolysis and partial conjugation. Normeperidine is about half as potent as meperidine, but it has twice the CNS stimulation effects.","type":"literal"}},
