{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00308","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"884.5003","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Primarily hepatic. Eight metabolites of ibutilide were detected in metabolic profiling of urine. These metabolites are thought to be formed primarily by o-oxidation followed by sequential b-oxidation of the heptyl side chain of ibutilide. Of the eight metabolites, only the o-hydroxy metabolite possesses class III electrophysiologic properties similar to that of ibutilide in an in vitro isolated rabbit myocardium model.","type":"literal"}},
