{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB01205","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"303.1019","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Hepatic. Flumazenil is completely (99%) metabolized. The major metabolites of flumazenil identified in urine are the de-ethylated free acid and its glucuronide conjugate.","type":"literal"}},
{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00849","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"246.1004","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Hepatic, primarily by the hepatic microsomal enzyme system. About 75% of a single oral dose of mephobarbital is metabolized to phenobarbital in 24 hours.","type":"literal"}},
