{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00275","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"558.2227","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Olmesartan is rapidly and completely bioactivated by ester hydrolysis to olmesartan during absorption from the gastrointestinal tract. There is virtually no further metabolism of olmesartan.","type":"literal"}},
{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00650","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"511.1128","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Hepatic and intestinal mucosal, the main metabolite being the active 5-methyltetrahydrofolate. Leucovorin is readily converted to another reduced folate, 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate, which acts to stabilize the binding of fluorodeoxyridylic acid to thymidylate synthase and thereby enhances the inhibition of this enzyme.","type":"literal"}},
{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00378","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"312.2089","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Metabolism is complete to a 20-dihydrodydrogesterone (DHD) metabolite.","type":"literal"}},
{"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB01101","type":"uri"},"mass":{"value":"359.1493","type":"literal"},"transform":{"value":"Metabolized by thymidine phosphorylase to fluoruracil.","type":"literal"}},
